           Turns on debugging via ssyysslloogg(3).

       uussee__aauutthhttookk
           When password changing enforce the module to use the new password
           provided by a previously stacked ppaasssswwoorrdd module (this is used in
           the example of the stacking of the ppaamm__ppaasssswwddqqcc module documented
           below).

       eennffoorrccee__ffoorr__rroooott
           If this option is set, the check is enforced for root, too.

       rreemmeemmbbeerr==_N
           The last _N passwords for each user are saved in
           /etc/security/opasswd. The default is _1_0. Value of _0 makes the
           module to keep the existing contents of the opasswd file unchanged.

       rreettrryy==_N
